  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nine dual-case prepositions",
     "texto": [
      "**An, auf, hinter, in, neben, über, unter, vor** and **zwischen** can take the dative or the accusative. To indicate location and answer **wo? (where?)**, the dative is used: **Das Buch liegt auf dem Tisch** (the book is on the table).",
      "The case doesn't depend on whether there is physical movement: it depends on whether a location or a destination or change of place is expressed. That's why you say **Ich laufe im Park** (I run inside the park, location) and **Ich laufe in den Park** (I run into the park, destination)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Contractions",
     "texto": [
      "With the dative, some combine: **in dem** → **im** (in the), **an dem** → **am** (next to the), **bei dem** → **beim**, **von dem** → **vom**.",
      "Examples: **im Wohnzimmer** (in the living room), **am Fenster** (next to the window)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Preposition",
